ivision-Coefficient-Forms-and-the-Artinian-Eisenbud-Green-Harris-Conjecture-September-23-2026.html#cor:characteristic-zero","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:3622da025283abd7d2f9788f37b5ac4bab2033b4e4605c17ea4403a72ad2c25a","file":"preprints/Commuting-Division-Coefficient-Forms-and-the-Artinian-Eisenbud-Green-Harris-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":92,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"53efe92db3fc1608531c2433254c183379ce51d138a04967fc17b12e14a09d10","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Commuting-Division-Coefficient-Forms-and-the-Artinian-Eisenbud-Green-Harris-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:3622da025283abd7d2f9788f37b5ac4bab2033b4e4605c17ea4403a72ad2c25a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Commuting-Division-Coefficient-Forms-and-the-Artinian-Eisenbud-Green-Harris-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L92"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:characteristic-zero}\nLet \\(F\\) be a field of characteristic zero, let\n\\(S_F=F[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]\\) be standard graded, and let\n\\[\n 1\\le c\\le n,\\qquad 2\\le a_1\\le\\cdots\\le a_c.\n\\]\nIf a homogeneous ideal \\(I\\subseteq S_F\\) contains a homogeneous regular\nsequence \\(f_1,\\ldots,f_c\\) with \\(\\deg f_i=a_i\\), there is a monomial ideal\n\\(J\\subseteq S_F\\) containing\n\\(P_F=(x_1^{a_1},\\ldots,x_c^{a_c})\\) such that\n\\[\n \\dim_F(S_F/J)_d=\\dim_F(S_F/I)_d\\qquad(d\\ge0).\n\\]\nMoreover, \\(J\\) may be chosen lex-plus-powers: in each degree its monomials\noutside \\(P_F\\) are the lexicographically greatest\n\\(\\dim_F I_d-\\dim_F(P_F)_d\\) monomials outside \\(P_F\\), for the order\n\\(x_1>\\cdots>x_n\\)."}
